     "type": "output_text",
     "text": "## A0 context model \u2014 Control timed tank filling\n\n**Scope:** Model the PLC control behavior for the customized Factory I/O tank scene. The plant and Modbus TCP communication provide the sensing and actuation mechanisms.\n\nThe context function is **A0 \u2014 Control timed tank filling**. Its decomposition consists of A1\u2013A4 below.\n\n### ICOM table\n\nSemicolon-separated entries represent distinct arrows. Rule-set names are noun phrases; their contents are defined below.\n\n| Node | Function | Inputs | Controls | Outputs | Mechanisms |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **A0** | **Control timed tank filling** | StartCommand signal; StopCommand signal; LSH signal; LSHH signal | TimerDuration; Initialization rules; Start-event rules; Filling-sequence rules; Stop-priority rules; Valve-output rules | fill_valve; discharge_valve | OpenPLC Runtime; PLC input sampling; PLC timer facility; Modbus TCP connection; Factory I/O tank scene |\n| **A1** | **Acquire command events and level states** | StartCommand signal; StopCommand signal; LSH signal; LSHH signal | Start-event rules; I/O mapping specification | start; stop; LSHH | PLC input sampling; Rising-edge detection memory; Modbus TCP connection |\n| **A2** | **Determine the filling step** | start; stop; LSHH; timer_done | Initialization rules; Filling-sequence rules; Stop-priority rules | Step state; Timer enable; Timer reset | OpenPLC Runtime; Sequence-state memory |\n| **A3** | **Measure the filling interval** | Timer enable; Timer reset | TimerDuration; Timer operating rules | timer_done | PLC timer facility; PLC scan execution |\n| **A4** | **Generate valve commands** | Step state; stop; LSHH; timer_done | Valve-output rules; Stop-priority rules; I/O mapping specification | fill_valve; discharge_valve | OpenPLC Runtime; PLC output image; Modbus TCP connection |\n\n**Additional context controls:** The **I/O mapping specification** and **Timer operating rules** used by the children are also controls on A0. They are listed separately here to keep the context-table entry readable.\n\n### Control-arrow definitions\n\n| Control arrow | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| **Initialization rules** | Step 0 is the initial state. Both valve commands are FALSE in step 0. |\n| **Start-event rules** | `start` is TRUE only for the scan in which a sampled rising edge of StartCommand is detected. A continuously held StartCommand does not generate repeated events. |\n| **Filling-sequence rules** | In step 0, `start` initiates the filling step. During filling, `timer_done` or `LSHH` terminates filling and returns the sequence to step 0. `LSH` has no transition or cutoff role in this task. |\n| **Stop-priority rules** | Whenever `stop` is TRUE, step 0 and FALSE valve commands take priority over every other condition. |\n| **Timer operating rules** | The timer starts with entry into the filling step. `timer_done` indicates expiration of TimerDuration for that filling interval. Leaving filling resets the timer so elapsed time does not carry into a subsequent fill. |\n| **Valve-output rules** | `fill_valve` is TRUE only while filling and while `stop`, `LSHH`, and `timer_done` are all FALSE. `discharge_valve` is always FALSE. Thus a high-high condition prevents an opening command even if it coincides with `start`. |\n| **I/O mapping specification** | Physical addresses and logical identifiers follow the mapping below. |\n\n### I/O and identifier mapping\n\nThe physical tag names identify boundary signals. The exact required vocabulary is used for logical receptivities and valve commands.\n\n| Physical tag or parameter | Address / type | Logical identifier or role |\n|---|---|---|\n| StartCommand | `%IX100.0 : BOOL` | `start` \u2014 one-scan press event generated by A1 |\n| StopCommand | `%IX100.1 : BOOL` | `stop` \u2014 TRUE whenever StopCommand is TRUE |\n| LSH | `%IX100.2 : BOOL` | `LSH` \u2014 target-level indication at 2.4 m; unused by the control sequence |\n| LSHH | `%IX100.3 : BOOL` | `LSHH` \u2014 overfill-limit indication at 2.7 m |\n| FillValve | `%QX100.0 : BOOL` | `fill_valve` \u2014 TRUE opens the valve |\n| DischargeValve | `%QX100.1 : BOOL` | `discharge_valve` \u2014 always FALSE |\n| TimerDuration | `TIME` | Timer-duration control |\n| Internal timer result | Internal BOOL | `timer_done` \u2014 filling timer elapsed |\n\n### Child-function connections\n\n- **A1 \u2192 A2:** `start`, `stop`, `LSHH`.\n- **A1 \u2192 A4:** `stop`, `LSHH`.\n- **A2 \u2192 A3:** **Timer enable**, **Timer reset**.\n- **A3 \u2192 A2 and A4:** `timer_done`.\n- **A2 \u2192 A4:** **Step state**.\n- **A4 \u2192 A0 boundary:** `fill_valve`, `discharge_valve`.\n\nThe **Step state** arrow carries either **step 0** or the **filling step**. The timer feedback represents state-dependent behavior across PLC scans, not a separate operating step.\n\n`LSH` terminates at A1 as an acquired but unused indication; it must not be substituted for `LSHH` or used to end the timed fill. All child boundary arrows are accounted for by the A0 inputs, controls, outputs, or mechanisms.",
